WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.920
The English army continues their advance.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.760
In order to stop them, 
the exiled French royal court in Chinon

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.150
attempted peace talks with Burgundy.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.030
However, Duke John I of Burgundy 
was outrageously murdered

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:21.740
during negotiations by radical 
factions within the royal family.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.440
{ryousha}The relationship between the two 
nations had become irreparable.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:31.750
Duke John I was succeeded 
by Philip the Good.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:37.450
{kanojo}She is currently heading to Chinon 
alone, on a top-secret mission.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:01:02.330
<b>#04 Who Was the Promise For</b>

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.570
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:26.170
She can only remain 
as Ulysses for three minutes.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.620
I have sinned, Your Majesty.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.340
I left the fighting to that man,

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.240
and I was waiting for her to calm down.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.080
Someone...

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.670
Please quiet down.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.480
I have no business with you.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.010
My employer only ordered me to...

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.820
obtain the Philosopher's Stone.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.200
Don't look down on us mercenaries!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.680
Look over here!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.910
Not even a greeting?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.670
Looks like that punk Montmorency 
really knew the princess!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.600
We've received our unpaid salary!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.570
Bring the booze!

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.060
Keep them coming!

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.240
What's wrong, Étienne?

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.560
Jeanne and others have been caught.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.360
What did you say?

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.820
Then, this money is...

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.420
It means don't get involved.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.200
My name is Girard.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:53.210
I'm about to butcher you like a rabbit,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.120
but please tell me how 
to transmute elixir before I do.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.920
The Philosopher's Stone 
is useless without the elixir.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.220
If you don't tell me the truth,

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.220
I'm going to have to mutilate 
the princess's beautiful face.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.480
Montmorency...

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.400
You have to baiser Montmorency.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.930
Hot elixir flows from his mouth.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:21.050
Oh? That's quite an amusing story.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.670
It's the truth.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:26.600
But don't hurt Montmorency.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.680
You can have my stone.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.160
Don't hurt anyone else.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.460
S-Someone...

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.420
Have you ever heard of someone

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:37.610
crying in agony after 
her throat had been slit?

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.670
Please remain quiet.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.370
Then your throat will be safe.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:48.640
I can't say we ever got along,

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.480
but I don't deserve this from a relative.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.870
Oh, but you do, my dear cousin.

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:58.020
The French royal family will not achieve 
victory through war tactics or strategy.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.760
It will be through politics.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.650
We will relinquish the French throne 
and Northern France to England,

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.800
which we've already lost.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.530
In exchange, we will secure territorial 
rights to the land south of Loire River,

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:12.540
and gain the status of 
"royal family of Southern France."

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.040
Explain it in a way that I can understand.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.990
Philip the Good will visit this castle.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.520
There is no hope of survival 
for the royal family

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.310
other than making peace with England.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.550
No one is more fit to serve 
as the mediator than her,

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.640
since both sides approve of her.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.770
I've spent an incredible amount 
of time and effort to make this happen.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.450
Yet here you are,

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:41.280
plotting to overthrow Princess Charlotte 
with your phony female saint!

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.320
Pathetic!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.060
You too, Richemont.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.320
Are you both trying to put 
an end to the royal family?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:46.940
Hold it.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.550
Did you come up with that plan on your own?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.370
As I thought.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.080
The Charlotte I know 
would never accept such defeat.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.940
Charlotte is no longer the girl you know.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.240
After seeing so much bloodshed 
as head of the royal family,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.500
Charlotte eventually lost all hope.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.180
Th-That's enough...

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.580
Shh.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:20.850
She secluded herself, and left all 
the decision making to La Tremoille.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.630
When I was stripped 
of the title of general,

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.120
she didn't offer to help.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:31.480
Charlotte ceased to believe in people, 
the future, and everything else.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.520
It's my fault.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.190
I didn't even offer a single word of 
encouragement in all these seven years.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.430
I'm to blame.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:46.420
Why you...

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:02.600
Not yet.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:06.150
I can't let it end yet!

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.610
That promise...

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.940
I can't give up on it!

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.870
Richemont, Charlotte, and Philip.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:20.220
They're my irreplaceable friends 
that I have to save now!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.210
What do you think you can do now?

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.480
Do you still remember?

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:33.660
Back then, I was the one who first said 
I wanted us to remain friends forever.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:37.600
Stay back. You're not used to fighting.

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.350
Richemont...

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.600
Fine. We'll take care of you first.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:45.860
Hand that over!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.400
Looks like I made it on time.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.510
The great female mercenary 
of Gascony, La Hire,

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:04.000
makes her grand appearance.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.760
You came to save us?

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.200
I didn't come to save you.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.720
I'm here to save Jeanne and Astaroth.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:10.890
Apparently.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.910
You dirty mercenary!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.260
We've already paid you!

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.200
Oh, you can have this back.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.010
Guys!

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.180
He's running away!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:46.230
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.740
Sorry.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:53.800
I made Your Majesty cry.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.770
I'm sorry.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.050
Well, then...

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.440
S-Someone!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.820
Someone help!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.920
Someone help!

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:14.900
That room?

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.700
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.110
Montmorency!

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.130
Jeanne! You were here?

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.960
Your employer has ran away.

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:30.710
Tell that to the man lying down there.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:34.620
You weren't hired by La Tremoille?

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:41.130
Hurry and shoot.

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.330
Keep quiet.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.910
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:49.290
<i>He'll slit Jeanne's throat 
the moment I pull the trigger.</i>

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.770
What are you after?

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.520
The Philosopher's Stone.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:54.220
What does that mean?

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.860
I'll explain later, Richemont.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:57.920
You can have the stone.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.750
This is the other half of the 
stone that's in Jeanne's body.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.460
If that's the case,

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:08.350
then it would've been quicker 
to kill you and take that instead.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.760
No, Montmorency!

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:11.470
I'll trade it for Jeanne.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.630
Swallow the stone, and get lost.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.390
You think I don't know that I would die 
if I swallowed the stone on its own?

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.360
This girl has already told me,

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.580
that elixir flows out of your mouth.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:30.400
Damn! There's no tricking you.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.660
Hold on! I'll soak the stone with elixir.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:43.420
So this is it!

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:52.510
I've become a Ulysses 
with power equal to Jeanne!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.090
I don't know about that.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:59.720
I didn't have a baiser with Jeanne
because I'm a pedophile.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.030
It evaporates right away 
when it comes in contact with air.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.060
In other words...

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:12.520
You swallowed the 
Philosopher's Stone on its own.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:15.230
You tricked me!

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:20.910
Jeanne!

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.330
I have so many questions.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.080
I expect so.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:29.100
I'd never imagined

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:32.520
the rumored female saint was a child 
who had swallowed the Philosopher's Stone.

00:11:32.520 --> 00:11:34.280
She's not just a child.

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:37.520
Even without the Philosopher's Stone,

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.560
Jeanne is a true saint.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:45.110
She cared more about me than 
her own life, even though we've just met.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.290
Montmorency.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.480
Philip?

00:12:15.590 --> 00:12:17.000
Excuse me...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.000
Your bill...

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.580
Worry not.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.380
Unpaid salary.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.050
Plus bonus!

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:33.770
It's been seven years.

00:12:35.970 --> 00:12:37.640
How have you been?

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:50.890
I came here with the intention 
to serve as a mediator for peace talks.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:56.020
Do you think the war will end if the French 
royal family surrenders to England?

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:58.200
It won't end.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:01.340
The royal family has many 
branches and relatives.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:05.530
They'll begin claiming 
that they are the true king,

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.300
and the world will become 
even more chaotic.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.480
Then what should we do?

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.440
If France unites as one...

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.560
Unites as one?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.840
Yeah.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:16.990
If the throne becomes incontestable...

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.320
If this country is bound by such unity,

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:22.100
then England will have to give up,
 and the war will end.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.420
To make that happen, the Duchy of Burgundy

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.710
needs to sign a truce with the French 
royal family and become allies.

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:31.580
We need your help.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.760
There's been too much bloodshed 
between the duchy and the royal family.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:39.600
The gap created between the duchy and 
the royal family will be bridged by Jeanne,

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.420
and the populace who support her.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.400
Also, I'll support you.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.260
I'm sure it's been hard for you.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.840
I'll never make you feel alone again, Philip.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.050
Montmorency...

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.160
Philip.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:15.240
Father?

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:19.870
Don't tell me you're thinking 
of allying with them.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:23.580
Allying with those who murdered your father?

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.890
No, Charlotte didn't murder you, Father...

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.850
This turmoil is an opportunity.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.900
Turn Burgundy into the most 
powerful empire in Europe.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:41.150
Bring your father's dream to fruition.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.640
I want elixir!

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.250
N-Not now.

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.340
I want it now!

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.470
There are so many people around here.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.660
We can do it later.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.990
Wait! No!

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.940
Wow!

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:07.420
I feel so rejuvenated!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.240
Elixir is so tasty!

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:12.410
Sheesh!

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.520
So you can use the Philosopher's Stone 
if you baiser with Montmorency?

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.310
Hey, Montmorency! 
I wouldn't mind if it's with you!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.240
Huh?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.580
Baiser with me now, and give me elixir!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:28.440
Then I can become Ulysses 
with the other half

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.720
of the Philosopher's Stone!

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:32.000
Wait a minute!

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:35.830
I can't let you baiser Montmorency, 
even if it's you, Charlotte!

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.230
Oh, come on!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:41.100
Your stuff is my stuff, 
and my stuff is your stuff, too!

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.460
No! No way!

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.640
Charlotte's boobs are big, so you're 
not allowed to baiser Montmorency!

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.120
No, no, no!

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.720
Hey, calm down, Jeanne!

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:54.540
She's still hyper because 
she used the Philosopher's Stone.

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.020
Jeanne is all the Ulysses we need.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:57.800
Huh?

00:15:57.800 --> 00:16:00.520
As long as Philip makes up his mind,

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.750
the war will be over without 
you having to become Ulysses.

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:06.480
It's so obvious.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.720
Don't tell me Richemont wants to become 
Ulysses and baiser Montmorency, too!

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:13.550
Hold on!

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:16.460
If you bow before me and say, 
"Please give me Montmorency,"

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.330
then I wouldn't mind giving him to you.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.330
No, uh...

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:22.280
Stop joking around!

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.770
I'm not joking.

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:26.510
Romance is as important as the war!

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:27.310
You guys...

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:29.000
Enough already!

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.280
What do you think the Philosopher's Stone is?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.920
It's not a toy!

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.920
Astaroth is right.

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.510
You can obtain great power, 
but there will be great losses, too.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:40.570
That's how the Philosopher's Stone works.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:43.500
I don't intend to let you two 
use the Philosopher's Stone.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.770
After all, if I wanted to,

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.620
I would've let Richemont swallow the 
Philosopher's Stone and gave her a baiser.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:54.890
I-I would absolutely refuse to 
baiser with you for that reason!

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:57.520
Oh? But you're not refusing baiser in itself?

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.420
No, no, no, no!

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:04.970
So? Have you made up your mind?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:09.950
If all four of us are together, 
then I can fight England.

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.150
We have Jeanne, too.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:11.950
Yeah.

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:14.000
Let's end the war together.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:17.800
Our promise must have 
been meant for this day!

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.930
Girard is from Burgundy.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.910
What did you just say?

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:30.940
Girard was acting on my 
father's wishes by himself.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.750
My father's wish was

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:36.520
to use the Philosopher's Stone to make 
Burgundy the most powerful empire.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.200
Philip?

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.720
I will also abide by his wishes.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.030
I'm sorry.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:44.250
I cannot fight alongside you.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.940
Philip has forgotten our promise.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.590
Montmorency?

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.350
<i>Your conviction and determination</i>

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.520
<i>to fulfill your duty brought 
on by this twisted fate...</i>

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.350
<i>I respect and admire it.</i>

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:10.110
<i>But Philip...</i>

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:13.360
<i>"Turning Burgundy into the most 
powerful empire in Europe."</i>

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:16.750
<i>Is that really your dream?</i>

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:17.880
Stay away!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.150
Forget your parents' ambitions!

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.380
We're supposed to always be friends!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.140
Get back!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.630
Montmorency.

00:18:56.560 --> 00:18:57.750
Philip...

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:02.300
This must be fate.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.870
I couldn't have done that if it weren't you.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:12.790
I have obtained elixir, Father.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.790
I, Charlotte, have made up my mind!

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.380
We will not surrender!

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:22.380
We will drive out the English army
 from the French territory,

00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:27.060
and achieve victory so complete that they 
will never even think of invading us again!

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.650
Her Majesty has reawakened.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:32.010
What happened?

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:32.860
Who knows?

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:37.100
It's fine that she's back, but we don't 
have the military forces anymore.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.400
Don't worry.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:40.650
The knight is right here!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:08.430
They say that lilies symbolize purity.

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:13.690
So Jeanne the Maiden, 
that flag suits you very well.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.890
Jeanne the Saint 
has lifted Her Majesty's spirits!

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.580
The Lord has not forsaken France!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:32.830
God bless France!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.210
Let's fight the invaders 
together, Your Majesty!

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:37.840
Thank you, everyone!

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.160
Thank you!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:43.220
I'll stand on the front line 
and drive away the English army!

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:45.470
Let's end the war!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.100
We're one step closer to utopia.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:53.900
Tell me...

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:58.570
Why are you working so hard 
to make the world a better place?

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.360
You don't seem to be 
a philanthropist, either.

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:04.990
Atonement.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:08.240
Montmorency!

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:12.730
Charlotte says she'll make 
you second in command!

00:21:12.730 --> 00:21:15.000
Come over here! Run!

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:27.740
I see.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:30.260
I understand the situation.

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:34.770
Even if Her Majesty 
Princess Charlotte approves,

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:39.180
a heretic becoming a knight... 
will not be approved by God.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:41.770
Please leave the rest to me.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:45.210
May justice prevail in the name of God.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.030
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>#05 Proof of Purity</b>

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:21.920
That bastard La Tremoille!

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.250
He claims Jeanne is tainted by the devil,

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:27.840
and wants to confirm her purity 
by checking her virginity!

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.690
Episode 5: "Proof of Purity."

00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:31.280
Hey! You guys in front of the TV!

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:32.990
Why are you cheering for La Tremoille?!

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:34.580
I'll kick your ass!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>"Delicious elixir flows out of his mouth"</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Use it when something is about 
to come out of a mouth!</b>
